,"title":5,"body":137,"description":465,"extension":466,"links":467,"meta":468,"navigation":469,"path":6,"seo":470,"stem":7,"__hash__":471},"docs\u002Fdocs\u002F01.introduction.md",{"type":138,"value":139,"toc":458},"minimark",[140,160,165,172,209,217,221,330,334,337,358,365,369,379,418,422],[141,142,143,147,148,151,152,155,156,159],"p",{},[144,145,146],"strong",{},"sched"," is a cron scheduler done right: ",[144,149,150],{},"reliable delivery",", ",[144,153,154],{},"run history",", and a\n",[144,157,158],{},"web UI"," — self-hosted, queue-based, polyglot-ready.",[161,162,164],"h2",{"id":163},"why-sched","Why sched",[141,166,167,168,171],{},"\"Fire and forget\" is not enough for a scheduler. sched's promise — ",[144,169,170],{},"the scheduler knows\neverything about every run",":",[173,174,175,187,193,199],"ul",{},[176,177,178,181,182,186],"li",{},[144,179,180],{},"Input"," — with what parameters the task was invoked (",[183,184,185],"code",{},"data",")",[176,188,189,192],{},[144,190,191],{},"Progress"," — 0–100 progress and captured stdout\u002Fstderr log",[176,194,195,198],{},[144,196,197],{},"Outcome"," — JSON result, error, artifacts (S3 keys, email receipts, URLs)",[176,200,201,204,205,208],{},[144,202,203],{},"Lifecycle"," — ",[183,206,207],{},"queued → running → succeeded | failed | cancelled",", timestamps, duration",[141,210,211,212,216],{},"Runs survive restarts, locks are reaped, and every run is recorded in the storage — SQLite\nby default, or MySQL\u002FMariaDB, Postgres or Mongo when history must live in an existing\ndatabase (each is a separate package, see ",[213,214,66],"a",{"href":215},"storage",").",[161,218,220],{"id":219},"key-features","Key features",[173,222,223,233,260,270,280,290,304,313,322],{},[176,224,225,228,229,232],{},[144,226,227],{},"Cron scheduling"," with timezone support (",[183,230,231],{},"tz",") and DST-safe next-run calculation",[176,234,235,238,239,242,243,151,245,151,248,151,251,151,254,151,257],{},[144,236,237],{},"Run history"," (",[183,240,241],{},"RunRecord","): ",[183,244,185],{},[183,246,247],{},"result",[183,249,250],{},"error",[183,252,253],{},"progress",[183,255,256],{},"log",[183,258,259],{},"artifacts",[176,261,262,265,266,269],{},[144,263,264],{},"Pluggable storage"," — SQLite first (in ",[183,267,268],{},"@schedjs\u002Fcore","), MySQL\u002FMariaDB, Postgres and\nMongo as separate adapter packages, all with a contract test-suite",[176,271,272,275,276,279],{},[144,273,274],{},"Polyglot runners"," — HTTP, Docker, and any custom runner you write against the ",[183,277,278],{},"Runner"," contract",[176,281,282,285,286,186],{},[144,283,284],{},"Embedded mode"," — schedule in-process functions with the internal runner; no daemon, no Docker (see ",[213,287,289],{"href":288},"quick-start#1-embedded-schedule-functions-in-process","quick start",[176,291,292,204,295,298,299,303],{},[144,293,294],{},"Retries with backoff",[183,296,297],{},"retry: { maxAttempts, backoffMs, multiplier }"," per task; a ",[300,301,302],"em",{},"persistent"," failure is one where retries ran out",[176,305,306,204,309,312],{},[144,307,308],{},"Idempotent dispatch",[183,310,311],{},"x-sched-run-id"," on the wire; workers dedupe by run id",[176,314,315,204,318,321],{},[144,316,317],{},"Async runs",[183,319,320],{},"202 accepted"," + polling for long-running jobs",[176,323,324,326,327,329],{},[144,325,108],{}," + ",[144,328,158],{}," (web components) — see runs, tasks, status",[161,331,333],{"id":332},"three-ways-to-run","Three ways to run",[141,335,336],{},"Pick by scale — the engine underneath is the same, so run history, retries and alerts\nwork on every path:",[338,339,340,346,352],"ol",{},[176,341,342,345],{},[144,343,344],{},"Embedded"," — schedule functions in-process, zero infra (SQLite file + handlers).",[176,347,348,351],{},[144,349,350],{},"Standalone daemon"," — own process with HTTP\u002FDocker workers, admin UI, alerts.",[176,353,354,357],{},[144,355,356],{},"Docker"," — the daemon in a container, compose-friendly, self-hosting.",[141,359,360,361,364],{},"See ",[213,362,9],{"href":363},"quick-start"," to run your first task on any of them.",[161,366,368],{"id":367},"architecture","Architecture",[370,371,376],"pre",{"className":372,"code":374,"language":375},[373],"language-text","            tasks.json (desired state)\n                    │ sync\n                    ▼\n   ┌────────────┐   tick\u002Fwatchdog\u002Fpoll    ┌───────────────────────────────┐\n   │   Engine   │ ──────────────────────▶ │      Runners (execution)      │\n   │ (scheduler)│   claim → run → record  │ http · docker · process · ssh │\n   │            │                         │ mcp · internal · custom       │\n   └─────┬──────┘                         └───────────────────────────────┘\n         │ storage seam\n         ▼\n   ┌───────────────────────┐    ┌──────────────────────────────────────┐\n   │        Storage        │    │  Daemon (CLI + Admin API + UI)       │\n   │ sqlite\u002Fmysql\u002Fpg\u002Fmongo │    │ --admin-port · SCHED_ADMIN_KEY       │\n   └───────────────────────┘    └──────────────────────────────────────┘\n","text",[183,377,374],{"__ignoreMap":378},"",[173,380,381,387,400,408],{},[176,382,383,386],{},[144,384,385],{},"Engine"," — deterministic tick loop + zombie watchdog over the storage seam. Claims due\ntasks, dispatches to the runner, records outcomes, reaps stale locks.",[176,388,389,391,392,395,396,399],{},[144,390,26],{}," — own ",[300,393,394],{},"how"," a task runs. HTTP (request\u002Fresponse, sync or ",[183,397,398],{},"accepted"," + poll),\nDocker (container spawn), or your own in-process function.",[176,401,402,404,405,407],{},[144,403,66],{}," — the ",[183,406,66],{}," contract: tasks, runs, locking. SQLite, MySQL\u002FMariaDB,\nPostgres and Mongo implement it.",[176,409,410,413,414,417],{},[144,411,412],{},"Daemon"," — loads ",[183,415,416],{},"tasks.json"," (desired state), syncs it, runs the engine, serves the\nadmin API and the web UI.",[161,419,421]